./" Manpage for mccv 
.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	mccv - mkdir directory, cp a file there, cd there, then edit the file in vim (the copy not the original)
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mccv source destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes a directory, copies a file there, cds to wherever it is now, then edits the copy in vim
	only edits the last file if you give multiple
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose.
	mv default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose
.SH EXAMPLES
	mccv hi.csv csvs
	mccv sdifji.py ../../ijsdif
.SH BUGS
	probably none
